+### [Progressive Ray Tracing](9723-progressive-ray-tracing.md)
+Computes only a subset of rays during interaction and progressively fills remaining pixels when interaction stops. Chose when interactive latency is critical and full refinement can occur offline; differs from checkerboard rendering by using spatial subsampling with interpolation rather than temporal blending of half-pixel traces.
 
-**Edge Cases:**
-*   **Motion:** If the camera or objects move significantly between frames, simple blending causes ghosting. This method assumes static or slowly moving scenes unless motion vectors are used to align the previous buffer (not detailed in [S1, unofficial]).
-*   **Convergence:** The image converges to the full-resolution result over two frames. Artifacts may be visible during the first frame after a scene change.
